Save this file to Project Knowledge. Copy/paste whichever prompt you need
directly into the chat when the situation calls for it.


1) CAMPAIGN RECAP PROMPT
(use when a chat is getting long and you want to continue in a new one)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Generate a full campaign state recap for continuing this Xianxia CYOA story in a new chat. Include, in compact YAML/markdown:
1. Current Status Window (full stats: identity, root, realm, vitals, karma, inventory, techniques, territory - latest values)
2. Character Profile - name, personality, defining trait, Dao Heart state, key relationships/Dao bonds
3. World State - current sect/faction standing, tier/position, known enemies & allies, active bounties or debts
4. Plot Threads - unresolved mysteries, pending promises, items/quests in progress
5. Recent Events - last 2-3 scenes in 1-2 sentences each, ending with exactly where we left off (location, time, what was about to happen)
6. Tone/Style Notes - reminder of the established mood, pacing, and any custom rules we've adjusted since Step 1-9 setup

Keep it dense and reference-only - no prose retelling, just the facts needed to resume without me re-explaining anything.


2) PURE TIME-SKIP PROMPT
(use when you know what you want to do and just want to skip ahead)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Time Skip Request] Advance the story forward by [X months/years] of in-world time, starting from the current timestamp. Summarize what happens during this period in a condensed montage (training progress, seclusion outcomes, background faction/world shifts, any pill toxicity or Karmic changes accrued) - 1-2 paragraphs, not a full narrated scene. Then resume normal scene-by-scene play at the new timestamp with an updated Status Window and fresh choices.


3) STRATEGIC PAUSE PROMPT (FULL VERSION)
(use when you're undecided on your next move and want options + fast-forward)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Strategic Pause] I'm undecided on my next move. Based on my current Status Window, surroundings, and active plot threads, briefly assess my situation (1 short paragraph). Then propose 3 distinct paths forward, each with:
- A one-line summary of the approach
- Approximate time cost to the next meaningful decision point
- Main risk and main reward, including expected Qi/Vitality/Mental State/Divine Sense drain, any Pill Toxicity or Karmic change, and any inventory items (pills, herbs, spirit stones, materials) likely to be consumed or gained

Once I pick one, compress the intervening time into a short montage and resume normal play at the new timestamp with a fully updated Status Window reflecting all resource costs, gains, and risks incurred - including specific inventory deductions/additions (item name, quantity, grade) for anything consumed, looted, crafted, or spent during the skipped period.

The world does not pause for me. During the skipped time, roll for background developments independent of my actions - rival disciples advancing, enemies making moves, allies facing their own struggles, sect/faction politics shifting, prices or resource scarcity changing, and any prior threats or debts progressing. Reflect these in the montage and/or as new plot threads upon return, even if they don't directly involve me yet.

If a major event would occur during the skip (ambush, tribulation, betrayal, life-altering discovery, or a decision with lasting consequences), stop the montage at that point instead of resolving it automatically - narrate up to it, then hand control back to me with a normal choice list.

Keep proposed time costs reasonable relative to my current realm/situation - flag if a path requires unusually long isolation.

Show Status Window 


QUICK REFERENCE (once these are established in a chat, you can just say):
- "I'm stuck, give me options and skip ahead" -> triggers prompt 3
- "Skip forward [X time]" -> triggers prompt 2
- "Give me a recap to continue elsewhere" -> triggers prompt 1
